From 2adae9a95cd200a0e3e120f9c57014c3fb31b952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:31:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/58] drm: wire TCL ACPI DSI supplies, display graph and
 firmware bridge

The staged display engine still lacks the DSI host, supplies, endpoint
graph and bridge required to reach the laptop panel. OEM firmware
already programs the LT8911EXB bridge, so this implementation makes that
handoff an explicit constraint.

Add the guarded DSI host and REFGEN/supply setup, extend the board's
I2C/pin description for the bridge, and construct the software-node
display graph. Add an LT8911 handoff bridge that checks the expected
register state and exposes the fixed panel mode; it does not perform a
complete bridge cold initialization. Include the display build
configuration and DSI interface changes used by this graph. Later
activation must still establish clocks and safely stop firmware scanout.
